<BaseLayout title="Nonstop Flights Singapore to London | SIN to LHR Direct" description="Guide to nonstop flights from Singapore to London. Singapore Airlines operates the world's longest commercial route, flying SIN to LHR nonstop in about 13 hours.">
<div class="breadcrumb"><div class="container"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span>Nonstop Flights: Singapore to London</span></div></div>
<section class="page-header">
  <div class="page-header-inner">
    <div class="page-eyebrow">Nonstop Route Guide</div>
    <h1>Nonstop Flights: Singapore to London</h1>
    <p>Singapore Airlines connects Changi Airport to London Heathrow nonstop in approximately 13 hours — one of the longest nonstop routes in the world by distance and widely regarded as one of the best premium flying experiences in the sky.</p>
    <div class="stat-strip">
      <div class="stat"><div class="stat-n">~13h</div><div class="stat-l">Flight time nonstop</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="stat-n">2 daily</div><div class="stat-l">Daily departures</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="stat-n">1 airline</div><div class="stat-l">Airline nonstop</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <SkyscannerWidget origin="Singapore" originCode="SIN" destination="London" destinationCode="LHR" />
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Airlines Flying Nonstop from Singapore to London</h2>
      <p>Singapore Airlines is the sole carrier operating nonstop flights between Singapore and London, and it is widely considered one of the world's finest airlines across all cabin classes.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Singapore Airlines</strong> — Operates the ultra-long-haul SIN-LHR route on the Airbus A350-900ULR (Ultra Long Range), a variant built specifically for extreme-distance flying. Offers Suites (first class), Business Class, Premium Economy, and Economy.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>The A350-900ULR: Built for Distance</h2>
      <p>The A350-900ULR is a purpose-built aircraft with additional fuel tanks and optimised aerodynamics for flights exceeding 13 hours. The aircraft cabin is designed for long-haul comfort, with lower cabin altitude and higher humidity than older jets — a genuine difference on a 13-hour sector.</p>
      <div class="tip-box"><p>Singapore Airlines' Premium Economy on ultra-long-haul sectors is one of the best value cabins in aviation — substantially more comfortable than Economy for a fraction of Business Class pricing.</p></div>
      <h2>Tips for Singapore to London Nonstop</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>KrisFlyer miles</strong> are among the most valuable airline currencies globally — Singapore to London in Business is a top redemption target.</li>
        <li><strong>Book early</strong> — this route fills quickly in both Business and Premium Economy. Award space opens 355 days out.</li>
        <li><strong>Sleep strategy</strong> — on the westbound leg departing Singapore in the morning, resist sleeping until evening UK time to fast-track jet lag recovery.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<div class="cta-strip"><div class="cta-strip-inner"><div><div class="cta-h">Find the Best Fare: Singapore to London</div><p class="cta-p">Search and compare fares on Singapore Airlines' flagship route.</p></div><a href="https://www.skyscanner.net/transport/flights/SIN/LHR/?adults=1" target="_blank" rel="noopener sponsored" class="btn-primary">Search on Skyscanner</a></div></div>
</BaseLayout>
